<body>
    <h1>Pitch and Sell — Exhaustive Feature &amp; Architecture Documentation</h1>
<p>This document serves as an exhaustive breakdown of absolutely every feature, screen, component, and architectural system built into the <strong>Pitch and Sell</strong> platform (Backend &amp; Mobile App).</p>
<hr>
<h2>1. Authentication &amp; Onboarding</h2>
<h3>Welcome Screen (UI/UX)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Dynamic Tabs:</strong> Switch smoothly between &#39;Sign In&#39; and &#39;Sign Up&#39; forms.</li>
<li><strong>Email Sign-In:</strong> Email and password fields with a visibility toggle (eye icon).</li>
<li><strong>Email Sign-Up:</strong> Comprehensive form capturing First Name, Last Name, Email, Phone Number, Password, and Profile Picture (via device gallery).</li>
<li><strong>Role Selection:</strong> Users must define their intent via a dropdown: <code>Buyer</code>, <code>Seller</code>, or <code>Both</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Social Connect:</strong> One-tap OAuth buttons for Google and Facebook.</li>
<li><strong>Validation:</strong> Strict frontend validation preventing empty fields and unchecked &quot;Terms &amp; Conditions&quot; boxes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Backend Auth Architecture</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Password Encryption:</strong> Uses <code>bcryptjs</code> to securely hash passwords before storing them in Supabase.</li>
<li><strong>JWT Sessions:</strong> Returns a secure JSON Web Token upon login.</li>
<li><strong>Google OAuth Verification:</strong> Backend utilizes <code>google-auth-library</code> to securely verify the <code>idToken</code> generated by the Flutter app.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>2. Main Navigation &amp; Core UI</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Persistent Bottom Navigation Bar:</strong> Gives access to Home (Feed), Explore (Search), Live/Upload, Inbox (Chats), and Profile.</li>
<li><strong>Global Role Switcher:</strong> A prominent toggle button in the top navigation allowing dual-role accounts to instantly switch between the &quot;Buyer&quot; experience and the &quot;Seller Dashboard&quot; without logging out.</li>
<li><strong>Shimmer Loaders:</strong> Premium skeleton loading animations are displayed while fetching data, completely replacing basic circular spinners.</li>
<li><strong>Deep Linking:</strong> Configured with <code>app_links</code> to intercept URLs (e.g., <code>https://pitch-and-sell-backend.onrender.com/product/123</code>) and open specific videos directly in the app.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>3. The Video Commerce Feed (TikTok-Style)</h2>
<h3>Video Player</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Vertical Paging:</strong> <code>PageView.builder</code> enables smooth, infinite vertical swiping.</li>
<li><strong>Pre-Caching Engine:</strong> Utilizes <code>flutter_cache_manager</code> to download and cache videos to the local device storage, eliminating buffering on subsequent views.</li>
<li><strong>Gestures:</strong> Tap to Play/Pause; Double-Tap to Like (triggers a floating, fading red heart animation).</li>
<li><strong>Lifecycle Management:</strong> Videos automatically pause when swiped away or when the app is minimized.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Interactive Overlays</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Sticky Header:</strong> Contains Search, Cart, unread Notification Bell, and the Buy/Sell mode toggle.</li>
<li><strong>Categories Bar:</strong> Horizontal scrollable pills to filter the feed (e.g., All, Fashion, Tech, Food, Handmade).</li>
<li><strong>Action Column:</strong> Floating buttons on the right side for Profile, Likes (with counter), Comments, and Share.</li>
<li><strong>Share:</strong> Copies a dynamic link to the clipboard to share the product externally.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Bottom Sheet Commerce Integration</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Product Details Sheet:</strong> Pulls up over the video displaying Name, Price, Discount/Old Price banner.</li>
<li><strong>Quantity Selector:</strong> Interactive (+/-) counter bounded between 1 and 24.</li>
<li><strong>Color/Variant Selector:</strong> Selectable pills for product variations (e.g., Black, Silver, Orange).</li>
<li><strong>Seller Verification Badge:</strong> Shows the seller&#39;s mini-profile and a &quot;Verified Business Seller&quot; green checkmark.</li>
<li><strong>Action Buttons:</strong> &quot;Add to Cart&quot; (shows a success toast) and &quot;Buy Now&quot; (routes directly to checkout).</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>4. E-Commerce Engine (Cart &amp; Checkout)</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cart Screen:</strong> Lists all accumulated products with individual quantity adjusters, subtotal calculations, and swipe-to-delete.</li>
<li><strong>Checkout Flow:</strong> <ul>
<li>Displays Order Summary.</li>
<li>Form for Shipping Address.</li>
<li>Payment Method selection (Cash on Delivery, Credit/Debit Card, Mobile Wallet).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Order Management Screen:</strong> Buyers can view &quot;Active&quot; and &quot;Past&quot; orders, track fulfillment status, and cancel pending orders.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>5. Seller Dashboard &amp; Analytics</h2>
<h3>Financial Ledger</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Available Balance:</strong> Large central display of withdrawable funds.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics Grid:</strong> 4 data cards tracking Gross Sales, Platform Fees, Net Earnings, and Total Paid Out.</li>
<li><strong>Audit Logs:</strong> A chronological list of every ledger event (e.g., <code>SALE_EARNING</code>, <code>WITHDRAWAL</code>), color-coded green for credits and red for debits.</li>
<li><strong>Payout System:</strong> Sellers can trigger a withdrawal request via a bottom sheet, selecting from Bank Account, EasyPaisa, or JazzCash, and providing their account details (Enforces a minimum PKR 500 threshold).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Content Management</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Upload Video Flow:</strong> A comprehensive form to publish a new pitch. Fields include Product Name, Price, Description, Category, Stock Qty, and a Video Picker. Includes a toggle to allow/disallow viewers from downloading the video.</li>
</ul>
<h3>AI Pitch Generator 🤖</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Inputs:</strong> Sellers input their Product Name, Key Selling Point (e.g., &quot;Active Noise Cancellation&quot;), Tone (Exciting vs. Professional), and Language (English or Roman Urdu).</li>
<li><strong>Output:</strong> Queries the backend AI route to generate a high-converting, 15-second video script formatted beautifully in monospace font.</li>
<li><strong>Recording Tips:</strong> Returns a bulleted list of camera and lighting tips based on the product type.</li>
<li><strong>Clipboard Integration:</strong> One-tap button to copy the script to the clipboard for teleprompter apps.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Boost Promotion Engine (Monetization)</h3>
<p>Sellers can pay to boost their video&#39;s algorithm ranking:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Standard Tier:</strong> 2x visibility multiplier for 24h (₨ 500).</li>
<li><strong>Premium Tier:</strong> 5x visibility multiplier for 72h (₨ 1,500).</li>
<li><strong>Elite Tier:</strong> 10x visibility multiplier for 7 days (₨ 5,000).</li>
<li><strong>Active Promos Tracker:</strong> A card on the dashboard showing the active boost&#39;s remaining time, total impressions, clicks, and orders generated.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>6. Social &amp; Real-Time Features</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Real-Time Chat:</strong> Powered by <code>Socket.io</code>. Users can join specific chat rooms, send messages instantly, and receive messages without pulling to refresh.</li>
<li><strong>Comments Section:</strong> A bottom sheet allowing users to read and post comments on specific videos.</li>
<li><strong>Notifications Screen:</strong> Central hub for order updates, likes, and messages.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>7. Backend Infrastructure &amp; Security</h2>
<h3>Technology Stack</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Server:</strong> Node.js with Express.js, written fully in strict TypeScript.</li>
<li><strong>Database:</strong> PostgreSQL hosted on Supabase (accessed via IPv4 Session Pooler).</li>
<li><strong>ORM:</strong> Prisma Client for strict database typing and migrations.</li>
<li><strong>Media Handling:</strong> <code>multer</code> configured for local/static file uploads (videos/images).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Security Architecture</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Rate Limiting:</strong> <code>express-rate-limit</code> caps every IP address to 100 requests per 15 minutes to prevent DDoS and Brute Force attacks.</li>
<li><strong>Helmet:</strong> Automatically injects 10+ HTTP security headers to prevent XSS, Clickjacking, and sniffing.</li>
<li><strong>Global Error Handling:</strong> All errors are caught by <code>error.middleware.ts</code>, preventing the server from crashing and ensuring the mobile app receives predictable <code>{ success: false, error: &quot;...&quot; }</code> JSON responses.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Server Routing &amp; APIs</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong><code>/api/auth</code></strong>: <code>POST /signup</code>, <code>POST /signin</code>, <code>POST /google</code>, <code>GET /me</code>, <code>PUT /profile</code>.</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/business</code></strong>: Endpoints for creating and updating the business/seller KYC profile.</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/products</code></strong>: <code>POST /</code> (Upload with Video), <code>GET /feed</code> (Algorithm logic for categories and search), <code>POST /video/:id/like</code>, <code>GET/POST /video/:id/comments</code>, <code>POST /:id/promote</code> (Boost).</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/orders</code></strong>: <code>POST /</code> (Create), <code>GET /</code> (Fetch by mode), <code>PATCH /:id/status</code>, <code>POST /:id/cancel</code>.</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/orders/ledger</code></strong>: Returns the seller&#39;s financial summary and audit trail.</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/orders/payout</code></strong>: Initiates a withdrawal request.</li>
<li><strong><code>/api/ai/generate-pitch</code></strong>: Handles LLM prompt construction for the Pitch Generator.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>8. Enterprise Readiness (Firebase)</h2>
<p>The Flutter app (<code>main.dart</code>) is pre-coded and prepared for integration with the Firebase suite:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics:</strong> Will automatically catch fatal Dart errors and native crashes, reporting them to the cloud.</li>
<li><strong>Firebase Analytics:</strong> Prepared to track screen views and video retention times.</li>
<li><strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM):</strong> Ready to accept permissions for native OS push notifications so sellers are alerted of new orders instantly.</li>
</ul>

</body>
